atlas model

architecture bitnet-address-ranker
  canonical_name BitNetAddressRanker
  family model
  domain Model / Addressable Candidate Narrowing
  layer model/execution
  semantic_question Given an AddressPlane survivor frontier and an admitted learned representation, which existing typed handles should be tried first without changing eligibility?
  purpose Consumes only an already mask-filtered AddressPlane forwarding result, requests a transient ResourceAdmission grant for a declared BitNet rerank workload, projects declared CandidateAdvertisement coordinates into content-digested EmbeddingProjections through the official BitNet execution surface, and preserves the whole ordered frontier plus each exact verifier and declared lowerer for bounded widening without repeating model work.
  maturity implemented
  owns BitNetRankRun
  owns AddressEmbeddingProjection
  consumes CandidateAdvertisement
  consumes ModelRepresentationPassport
  publishes RankedCandidateFrontier
  node_types BitNetRankRun
  node_types AddressEmbeddingProjection
  node_types RankedCandidateFrontier
  edge_types reorders
  edge_types projected_from
  invariant BitNet consumes only AddressPlane survivors and cannot add a candidate that deterministic forwarding rejected
  invariant every ranked record retains its original typed candidate kind, exact verifier and lowerer reference
  invariant an initial top-k is a bounded attempt slice; the complete stored frontier supports later widening after an exact rejection
  invariant only a measured ADMIT ModelRepresentationPassport may hand a ranked slice to declared lowerer lanes; DEFER is shadow-only
  invariant ResourceAdmission grants are transient physical execution leases released after ranked-frontier persistence; neither a grant nor a released grant changes candidate eligibility or model preservation standing
  invariant a persisted BitNetRankRun can emit representation-use evidence only from its stored source and vector digests; its gate state is preserved verbatim and a verifier reference is never counted as an exact-owner query
  forbidden_inference rank -> selection, semantic truth, availability, authority, evidence, proof, commitment, payment, or effect
  forbidden_inference top-k omission -> candidate impossibility or target failure
  forbidden_inference stored EmbeddingProjection -> owner fact or comparable vector without its representation passport
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBitNet/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBitNet/Makefile
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tools/estate-refresh.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBitNet/results/2026-09-12-bitnet-thread-scaling.json
  internal_calculus the embedding source is named by the caller and not implied by the transport: an HTTP endpoint, or the bitnet.cpp binary invoked directly. Both were in the usage string and only the endpoint was reachable -- the direct path was written, compiled, and never called from main, which -Wunused-function turns into a build failure the moment anything else in the file moves, and did
  internal_calculus the embedding thread count is measured rather than assumed. One thread was compiled in, which is the honest number to write before measuring; four is 2.49x faster on this host and eight is slower than four, because there are four performance cores and oversubscribing them costs more than it buys
  invariant a measurement establishes only what it measured. Latency, throughput, and one owner-predicate coverage curve do not move the passport, because ADMIT requires a preservation envelope across the declared retrieval families
  cannot_infer a faster embedding -> a better ranking; a thread count changes how long the model takes to say the same thing
  cannot_infer this host's optimum -> another host's; the default is overridable because the next execution phenotype will answer differently
  cannot_infer a SHADOW reorder over a real frontier -> a frontier anyone may act on; SHADOW is what DEFER plus --diagnostic produces and it hands nothing to a lowerer
  witness cmd/BonfyreBitNet/results/2026-09-12-bitnet-thread-scaling.json records the run the known_gap said was missing: 92 real AddressPlane survivors from a 4,891 population embedded at 1.79s per candidate single-threaded, returning 94,208 floats, plus a thread sweep at 1, 4 and 8 over a 24-candidate subset
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBitNet/results/2026-09-12-addressplane-ranking-quality.json
  invariant the passport is refused on measurement, not on absence of it. DEFER was correct before because nothing had been measured; it is correct now because something was, and the something was negative
  cannot_infer a deterministic frontier that did its job -> a learned ordering that did; all 92 survivors carried the required coordinate and the model still put three specifications above the first weather source
  witness cmd/BonfyreBitNet/results/2026-09-12-addressplane-ranking-quality.json measures the ranking the previous gap left unmeasured: over a real 92-survivor frontier, machine_protocol specifications are 16 percent of the population and 80 percent of the top five, roughly five times their base rate, and the first actual weather source lands at rank 3
  witness cmd/BonfyreBitNet/tests/cpp_path_test.sh proves the direct embedding source is reachable rather than merely present: naming --bitnet-cpp without --endpoint must fail as an embedding failure and never as a usage error
  witness cmd/BonfyreBitNet/tests/contract_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreBitNet/results/2026-09-12-addressplane-weather-shadow.json
  witness cmd/BonfyreBitNet/results/2026-09-12-addressplane-protocol-handoff.json
  witness /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/estate/representation-evidence.jsonl is atomically emitted from the persisted bitnet:1789271781 92-candidate rank run; /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/estate/bitnet-exact-owner-evidence.jsonl then records 92 separate native ForeignTwin queries over that same persisted frontier, retaining SHADOW on every representation record and reporting only two retained observations
  interacts addressplane-survivors-reorder-through-bitnet
  known_gap the unmodified official Microsoft BitNet embedding checkout at release-bitnet-embedding-0.6b-270m was rebuilt on this ARM host on 2026-09-12 and failed to link llama-embedding because dequantize_row_i2_s and quantize_i2_s have no ARM implementation; Microsoft documents the I2_S embedding releases as ARM-unsupported. The native ranker can now invoke the separately declared bitnet.cpp CLI path directly, reject non-finite output, and retain a bounded SHADOW frontier from the patched ARM diagnostic build, but that build remains SHADOW only. A deliberately isolated ADMIT mirror has exercised the generic ProtocolCommons handoff through the declared native ProtocolCompiler consumer, but it is not a production admission. Full-frontier latency and throughput are now measured on this host and recorded beside this entry; preservation recall, warm-worker pooling and concurrent capacity remain unmeasured, and those are the ones ADMIT actually turns on. The release build does embed here -- NEON, ARM_FMA, MATMUL_INT8 and DOTPROD all report active -- so what is unestablished is an unmodified upstream ARM build, not whether this host can produce embeddings at all.
  witness cmd/BonfyreBitNet/tests/drive_fitness_test.sh
  forbidden_inference a ranker whose bottom-k looks better than its top-k -> a useful ranker inverted; that is one query fitted, not a signal earned
  invariant the learned ordering does not decide what enters a bounded search. A subset lattice costs one branch per subset, so something must choose the k that enter, and on the persisted 92-survivor run BitNet is worse than drawing at random: the frontier is 84 percent reachable services, its top-16 is 69 percent, and 91 percent of random draws of 16 beat it
  known_gap the ranking is anti-correlated with usability on this frontier, not merely uninformative. Its bottom-16 is 88 percent services against an 84 percent base rate while its top-16 is 69 percent, so the model is finding something and ordering it backwards for this query. The entry already said three specifications outranked the first weather source; the consequence is now attached, which is that a SHADOW representation has not earned the right to spend a deterministic frontier's budget.
